        "order": 6,
        "cliff": "a robot with no manipulators is STR 0 and DEX 0",
        "teaches": [
          "manipulators[] is where a robot's Strength and Dexterity come from: each limb has a count, a size and the two scores it gives.",
          "locomotion[] is how it moves, and exactly one entry should be primary.",
          "brain.grade and brain.intellect are what it can decide, and traveller.enabled is what turns the six Traveller characteristics on.",
          "slots.removed is stored and slots.total derives; options[] is what has been fitted into them."
        ],
        "trap": "Only education.base and social.base are authored. hits, strength, dexterity, endurance and intellect are all PROJECTIONS into .auto from size, manipulators, agilityEnhancement, endurance and brain — a base written on any of those five silently ADDS to the projection. And the six show flags below are written by hand because _preCreate never runs for a packed document, exactly as with an npc."
      }
    }
  },
